{"abstract":"Microworlds have been proposed as an educational approach for engaging students and increasing motivation. However, the use of microworlds has largely been studied in the initial phases of learning to program (or entire courses). We adopted a microworld project at the end of our CS1 course to investigate its use in teaching students composition and creation of larger programs rather than initial familiarity with programming constructs. We here compare the impact of using a scaffolded, microworld project over a (previously used) non-scaffolded, non-microworld project. Based on data from N=303 students exposed to the two kinds of projects (145 in 2022 vs 158 in 2023), we compare the two cohorts according to a test of learning (TOL) based on the final exam grades. In 2023, we studied the impact further by considering the feel of learning (FOL) based on a qualitative student survey. The results show that the student grade-point average (TOL) increased significantly when we adopted the microworld project. Further, the microworld project appears to produce a high FOL.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nicolajsen, Sebastian Mateos","Caspersen, Michael E.","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-806846"],"event":{"end":"2025-03-01","place":"Pittsburgh, us","start":"2025-02-26","title":"56th Annual SIGCSE Technical Symposium on Computer Science Education, SIGCSE TS 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Introductory programming","Project","Scaffolding"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circle of life microworld project at the end of cs000000000001","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3641554.3701808","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-806846","identifier":[{"id":"86000243901","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7eeca7b7-ece7-47ee-9804-824fd6a5fe76"],"keyword":["Introductory programming","microworld","project","scaffolding"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B69BF8911AF8E753FD6A6C09319EF68B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3641554.3701808","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, It-vest - networking universities"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Mateos","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","name":"Nicolajsen, Sebastian Mateos","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael E.","key":"caspersenpau","last":"Caspersen","locid":"12999231-9347-4672-b899-4833b65ba9f8","name":"Caspersen, Michael E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","name":"Brabrand, Claus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3641554.3701808","eisbn":["9798400705311"],"pages":"854-860","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"SIGCSE TS 2025 - Proceedings of the 56th ACM Technical Symposium on Computer Science Education","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000243901"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7eeca7b7-ece7-47ee-9804-824fd6a5fe76"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Circle of Life : Microworld Project at the End of CS1","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-806846","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The underrepresentation of women in IT has been a long-standing issue. Research has shown that women’s first experience with computing education is vital in shaping their perception of the field and their perception of who “belongs” to it. In this Danish case study, we examine gender representation in the subject Informatics, which is the first mandatory, formal introduction to computing education for many students in Denmark. Across 25% of all Danish HHX high schools, we assess the teaching materials on parameters of gender representation in pronouns, names, images, audio/video material, and potential role models. Our results suggest an overall underrepresentation of women in textual and audio/video material, but not in images. We also find an overall absence of female role models, and a tendency for the materials to feature younger female role models than their male counterparts. We conclude with concrete recommendations for authors and publishers of teaching materials for ICT on the high school level.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Christensen, Ingrid Maria","Marcher, Melissa Høegh","Inie, Nanna","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759398"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computing education"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"invisible women in it examining gender representation in k 000000000012 ict teaching materials","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3632620.3671111","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759398","identifier":[{"id":"85202896996","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-426120e3-a659-422b-8a15-5d2df9a8fb9c"],"keyword":["Computing education"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D91C5B59EF21BE309DC78BD37F6482D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3632620.3671111","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3632620.3671111","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid Maria","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Ingrid Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Melissa Høegh","key":"marcherpau","last":"Marcher","locid":"2f4daeb6-5872-4c86-8f2d-5c5ffc3dd5fa","name":"Marcher, Melissa Høegh","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"dennypedh","last":"Denny","name":"Denny, Paul","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Leo","key":"porterpedh","last":"Porter","name":"Porter, Leo","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Margaret","key":"hamiltonpedh","last":"Hamilton","name":"Hamilton, Margaret","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Briana","key":"morrisonpedh","last":"Morrison","name":"Morrison, Briana","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3632620.3671111","eisbn":["9798400704758"],"pages":"246-262","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Conference on International Computing Education Research (ICER 2024)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85202896996"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-426120e3-a659-422b-8a15-5d2df9a8fb9c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Invisible Women in IT: Examining Gender Representation in K-12 ICT Teaching Materials","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759398","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This research-to-practice paper shows how to visualize the conceptual framework of object-oriented programming. 'Classes' and 'objects' (from the solution domain) are respectively visualized as 'phenomena' and 'concepts' (from the problem domain), thereby visualizing the connection between code and reality. In the spirit of bringing research-to-practice, we implemented a prototype programming environment for Java called 'SHowMyCODE' based on this conceptual visualization. We report on a controlled experiment involving N=138 introductory programming (CS1) students. The experiment involves three tasks with progression (USE, Modify, and Create) and compares a treatment group with the reality-code visualization vs a control group without the visualization. The results show that, for Use tasks, students are faster (but not more accurate) when using the reality-code visualisation. In contrast, for Create tasks, learners are more accurate (but not faster) when using the reality visualisation. Finally, we report that students appear to value a visualization that shows the reality-code connection above a generic visualization without this connection.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Staugaard, Jakob","Bennedsen, Jens","Seidl, Christoph","Nicolajsen, Sebastian","Fink, Mathias","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-806917"],"event":{"end":"2024-10-16","place":"Washington, us","start":"2024-10-13","title":"54th IEEE Frontiers in Education Conference, FIE 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Brabrand, Claus","Fink, Mathias","Nicolajsen, Sebastian","Seidl, Christoph","Staugaard, Jakob"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"visualizing the conceptual framework of object orientation for novice programmers","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105000619540","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-806917","identifier":[{"id":"105000619540","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-880b75f1-f78f-4d90-9010-9361ef27e49f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F6FD2B2C71079CE7A9604864FDF6D164"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering - Software Engineering & Computing systems - Edison"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"staugaardpau","last":"Staugaard","name":"Staugaard, Jakob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"bennedsenpau","last":"Bennedsen","locid":"acc52e24-257f-4176-aed2-1e9110da5dc9","name":"Bennedsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0003-3014-7567","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph","key":"seidlpau","last":"Seidl","name":"Seidl, Christoph","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","name":"Nicolajsen, Sebastian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"finkpau","last":"Fink","name":"Fink, Mathias","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","name":"Brabrand, Claus","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/fie61694.2024.10893141","eisbn":["9798350351507"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2024 IEEE Frontiers in Education Conference, FIE 2024 - Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105000619540"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-880b75f1-f78f-4d90-9010-9361ef27e49f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Visualizing the Conceptual Framework of Object Orientation for Novice Programmers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-806917","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Abundant research has investigated gender differ- ences from the perspective of the individual, but little research has explored gender differences from a group perspective. This paper presents a survey-based quantitative exploration of gender differences when N=138 students working in smaller (3 stu- dents) groups that are either men-majority (WMM) or men- only (MMM). The study was conducted during four weeks of CS1 project work, and the investigation focused on student struggle, task division, group satisfaction, and course outcomes. We observed four significant gender differences: (i) Many women students express a lack of confidence early in the project work, as do many men students that are part of mixed-gender (WMM) groups, but not men that are part of men-only (MMM) groups; (ii) In men-majority groups, women perform more ‘non- technical’ tasks than men (e.g., analysis, design, and report editing); and (iii) women students in men-majority groups are less satisfied with several aspects of the group work than men students in the same groups. These findings add to our understanding of group dynamics and collaboration (including what to avoid and where to pay extra attention) when assigning projects in smaller groups in computing education.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Westh, Bjørn Hjorth","Inie, Nanna","Barkhuus, Louise","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718933"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computing education","Confidence in project work","Gender differences","Group dynamics","Group satisfaction","Men majority groups","Mixed gender groups","Non technical tasks","Project work outcomes","Task division"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gender differences in the group dynamics of smaller cs000000000001 project groups","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102753129/FIE-2023-struggle_pdf.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project is partially funded by DIREC P31 with the intention of uncovering knowledge important for the recruitment and retention of students in Computer Science. One recurring discussion is how to form student groups and whether to let students form groups autonomously or to have course instructors form groups (and on which basis). This study was part of an initiative to understand how these groups work in practice, in order to be able to make evidence-based recommendations and decisions about this in the future."],"id":"S01-000.00-718933","ids":["itu-f48d14a6-4f0b-4ef6-85f9-64b989c0ebb1"],"keyword":["Computing education","Confidence in project work","Gender differences","Group dynamics","Group satisfaction","Men-majority groups","Mixed-gender groups","Non-technical tasks","Project work outcomes","Task division"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-61C0194325C7E4E2D053065FF7A5E20D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102753129/FIE-2023-struggle_pdf.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ccer.itu.dk/-/media/86E7BD9D7CD147E3AE014795C9AE42D3.ashx","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjørn Hjorth","key":"westhpau","last":"Westh","name":"Westh, Bjørn Hjorth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"place":"College Station, Texas, USA","status":"p","title":"IEEE ASEE Frontiers in Education Conference 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f48d14a6-4f0b-4ef6-85f9-64b989c0ebb1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gender Differences in the Group Dynamics of Smaller CS1 Project Groups","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718933","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"When humans are exposed to environmental and physical stressors, cognitive performance is degraded. Even though several studies have examined the effect of various stressors individually, there are limited studies comparing the impact of different types. This study examined the effects of Heat, Noise, and Alcohol on cognitive performance during two programming tasks to quantify the impact of stressors on novice programmers. The experiment enrolled N=100 university student volunteers for a between-subjects experiment. Participants were randomly assigned to one of four conditions (M=25): a room with at 38 °C (100 °F), a room with conversational noise around 80 dBA, a blood alcohol content of 1.0‰, or a base condition. Two programming tasks were administered: one analysis task (reading programs) and one synthesis task (writing programs), taking about half an hour to complete in total. Short-term exposure to heat appears to not significantly affect neither reading nor writing programs; conversational noise significantly impacts analytical tasks but not synthesis tasks; while alcohol significantly worsens performance in both analytical and synthesis tasks. To provide a tangible summary for decision-makers able to influence conditions for novice programmers, an approximated comparison is provided, which “translates” negative cognitive effects of heat, noise, and alcohol to one another.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Brabrand, Claus","Tell, Paolo","Inie, Nanna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718852"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cognitive performance","Environmental stressors","Physical stressors","Programming","Software Engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"programming under the influence on the effect of heat noise and alcohol on novice programmers","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102793509/Programming_under_the_influence_On_the_effect_of_Heat_Noise_and_Alcohol_on_novice_programmers.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718852","identifier":[{"id":"85182417093","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-492a7d2d-58f2-4663-8c3b-5d2f30baa6f7"],"keyword":["Cognitive performance","Environmental stressors","Physical stressors","Programming","Software engineering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A5EEDA45CB17786CF6EE1AD86A422E1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102793509/Programming_under_the_influence_On_the_effect_of_Heat_Noise_and_Alcohol_on_novice_programmers.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"tellpau","last":"Tell","locid":"2b8ff3a4-e9b0-403d-8bd8-1bf26121c234","name":"Tell, Paolo","orcid":"0000-0001-7391-0046","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jss.2023.111887","issn":["01641212","18731228"],"issn_org":["01641212"],"issue":"111887","journal":"Journal of Systems and Software","paperid":"111887","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Systems and Software","volume":"210"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182417093"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-492a7d2d-58f2-4663-8c3b-5d2f30baa6f7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Programming under the influence: On the effect of Heat, Noise, and Alcohol on Novice programmers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718852","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Previous work demonstrates that students without prior program- ming experience are worse off than their programming experienced peers in terms of both Introductory Programming (CS1) grades and dropout rates. Many universities, therefore, offer an onboarding (CS0) course aimed at bridging the programming experience gap by teaching the basics of programming to inexperienced students. This paper reports on the effects of providing a three-day elective onboarding course over a period of five years (2016–2020), involving a total of N=798 software development students at the IT University of Copenhagen. The paper compares 271 students who attended versus a baseline of 527 who did not attend the onboarding course. The results show that programming inexperienced students are indeed able to “catch up” to the level of their experienced peers both in terms of CS1 grades and dropout rates. Aside from objectively increasing competence, the onboarding also increases confidence, self-efficacy and diminishes insecurities, according to onboarded participants. Finally, the results suggest that onboarding has the potential to increase the diversity of students.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Grabarczyk, Pawel","Nicolajsen, Sebastian Mateos","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383588"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Competence","Computer Science","Computing","Confidence","Diversity","Dropout","Education","Gender","Grades","Onboarding","Programming","Self efficacy","Software development"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the effect of onboarding computing students without programming confidence or experience","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://ccer.itu.dk/-/media/80BCA0BC6DD8438DA566DD33265AED57.ashx","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383588","identifier":[{"id":"85142937486","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9f5d636e-4b5e-4c7f-8528-219c53cee961"],"keyword":["Diversity","Gender","competence","computer science,","computing","confidence","dropout","education","grades","onboarding","programming","self-efficacy","software development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B9546D48150984B5728729F380CE405"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://ccer.itu.dk/-/media/80BCA0BC6DD8438DA566DD33265AED57.ashx","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pawel","key":"grabarczykpau","last":"Grabarczyk","locid":"42147e05-f94c-471d-a889-c57a01e4bdd0","name":"Grabarczyk, Pawel","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-7474","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Mateos","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"e175684d-abc3-4ee4-9a12-af6c611e47c0","name":"Nicolajsen, Sebastian Mateos","orcid":"0000-0002-3498-0970","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3564721.3564724","eisbn":["9781450396165"],"place":"Koli, Finland","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM Proceedings of the Koli Calling International Conference on Computing Education Research","status":"p","title":"Koli Calling '22: 22nd Koli Calling International Conference on Computing Education Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142937486"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9f5d636e-4b5e-4c7f-8528-219c53cee961"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On the Effect of Onboarding Computing Students without Programming-Confidence or -Experience","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383588","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Every month, 6% of Danish nursing home residents are admitted to hospital. However, these admissions might have limited benefits and are associated with an increased risk of complications. We initiated a new mobile service comprising consultants performing emergency care in nursing homes. Objective: Describe the new service, the recipients of this service, hospital admission patterns and 90-day mortality. Design: A descriptive observational study. Model: When an ambulance is requested to a nursing home, the emergency medical dispatch centre simultaneously dispatches a consultant from the emergency department who will provide an emergency evaluation and decisions regarding treatment at the scene in collaboration with municipal acute care nurses. Method: We describe the characteristics of all nursing home contacts from 1st November 2020 to 31st December 2021. The outcome measures were hospital admissions and 90-day mortality. Data were extracted from the patients' electronic hospital records and prospectively registered data. Results: We identified 638 contacts (495 individuals). The new service had a median of two (interquartile range: 2-3) new contacts per day. The most frequent diagnoses were related to infections, unspecific symptoms, falls, trauma and neurologic disease. Seven out of eight residents remained at home following treatment, 20% had an unplanned hospital admission within 30 days and 90-day mortality was 36.4%. Conclusion: Transitioning emergency care from hospitals to nursing homes could present an opportunity for providing optimised care to a vulnerable population and limiting unnecessary transfers and admissions to hospitals.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Udesen, Stine Emilie Junker","Rasmussen, Claus-Henrik","Mikkelsen, Søren","Andersen, Nina","Brabrand, Mikkel","Lassen, Annmarie Touborg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671496"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Lassen, Annmarie Touborg"],"keyword":["Acute care","Emergency care","Emergency medicine","Nursing Homes","Nursing home residents","Older people"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Odense Kommune"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mobile emergency department care to nursing home residents a novel outreach service","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ageing/afad025","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-671496","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9978309","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85153348833","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36861182","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-1a111f65-2590-4060-95fc-b2f0be454770"],"keyword":["acute care","aged care facilities","emergency care","emergency medicine","nursing home residents","nursing homes","older people","outreach service"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9CD66208BF3774E5F45A73A5456E91FC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/228592196/afad025.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ageing/afad025","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Emergency Medicine (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Odense Kommune"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Emilie Junker","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","locid":"7552db96-a59d-4955-a83d-fde78472d168","name":"Udesen, Stine Emilie Junker","orcid":"0000-0002-5962-514X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus Henrik","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3d4aa700-141d-4c3c-bfc5-d2d368cce808","name":"Rasmussen, Claus-Henrik","name_org":"Rasmussen, Claus Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"7df86a29-c6dc-4919-a9f9-6f5c23591e1d","name":"Mikkelsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-5187-7027","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Nina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"96dae706-4310-46de-ac4f-447df19289f6","name":"Brabrand, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0002-3340-8251","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annmarie Touborg","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"80e651b5-e70f-43e0-baf8-e88335ac10b8","name":"Lassen, Annmarie Touborg","orcid":"0000-0003-4942-6152","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36861182"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ageing/afad025","issn":["00020729","14682834"],"issn_org":["14682834"],"issue":"3","journal":"Age and Ageing","paperid":"afad025","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Age and Ageing","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153348833"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1a111f65-2590-4060-95fc-b2f0be454770"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Mobile emergency department care to nursing home residents : a novel outreach service","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671496","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Existing research does not quantify and compare the differences be- tween automated and manual assessment in the context of feedback on programming assignments. This makes it hard to reason about the effects of adopting automated assessment at the expense of man- ual assessment. Based on a controlled experiment involving N=117 undergraduate first-semester CS1 students, we compare the effects of having access to feedback from: i) only automated assessment, ii) only manual assessment (in the form of teaching assistants), and iii) both automated as well as manual assessment. The three conditions are compared in terms of (objective) task effectiveness and from a (subjective) student perspective. The experiment demonstrates that having access to both forms of assessment (automated and manual) is superior both from a task effectiveness as well as a student perspective. We also find that the two forms of assessment are complementary: automated assess- ment appears to be better in terms of task effectiveness; whereas manual assessment appears to be better from a student perspec- tive. Further, we found that automated assessment appears to be working better for men than women, who are significantly more in- clined towards manual assessment. We then perform a cost/benefit analysis which leads to the identification of four equilibria that appropriately balance costs and benefits. Finally, this gives rise to four recommendations of when to use which kind or combination of feedback (manual and/or automated), depending on the num- ber of students and the amount of per-student resources available. These observations provide educators with evidence-based justifi- cation for budget requests and considerations on when to (not) use automated assessment.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kristiansen, Nynne Grauslund","Nicolajsen, Sebastian Mateos","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718869"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automated assessment","Feedback effectiveness","Manual assessment","Programming assignments","Student perspective"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feedback on student programming exercises teaching assistants vs automated assessment tool","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.itu.dk/people/brabrand/Koli-2023.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718869","ids":["itu-73bdc3b1-ff2f-4547-bcf0-9feb2aa022de"],"keyword":["Automated assessment","Feedback effectiveness","Manual assessment","Programming assignments","Student perspective"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-EBFE0A3940F023DE7AFBAB82356DC527"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.itu.dk/people/brabrand/Koli-2023.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nynne Grauslund","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Nynne Grauslund","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Mateos","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"e175684d-abc3-4ee4-9a12-af6c611e47c0","name":"Nicolajsen, Sebastian Mateos","orcid":"0000-0002-3498-0970","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"place":"Koli, Finland","status":"p","title":"ACM Proceedings of the 22nd Koli Calling International Conference on Computing Education Research (Koli 2023)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-73bdc3b1-ff2f-4547-bcf0-9feb2aa022de"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Feedback on Student Programming Exercises: Teaching Assistants vs Automated Assessment Tool","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718869","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Dette dokument indeholder en række anbefalinger til indførsel af teknologiforståelse i uddannelse af lærere og andet pædagogisk personale i folkeskolen. Konkret drejer det sig om teknologiforståelse som selvstændigt fag og som element i de eksisterende fag mate-matik, billedkunst og håndværk og design.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Andersen, Lars Bo","Brabrand, Claus","Buhl, Mie","Caprani, Ole","Georgesen, Marianne","Hachmann, Roland","Hjorth, Mikkel","Jørnø, Rasmus","Køhrsen, Louis","Misfeldt, Morten","Toft Nørgaard, Rikke","Nortvig, Anne-Mette","Middelboe Rehder, Mads"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-054782"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Lars Bo"],"level":"com","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-UCS","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-UCN","DI-UC-UCS","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anbefalinger til indførelse af teknologiforståelse i uddannelse af lærere og andet pædagogisk personale","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/472494130/gsk_teknologiforst_else_Slutrapport_anbefalinger_til_uddannelse_af_l_rere_og_p_dagoger.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-054782","ids":["aau-10310147-5b0f-481d-b11c-4561605c50f5"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3A8E33284DDC2046D09513F1EF484D46"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/472494130/gsk_teknologiforst_else_Slutrapport_anbefalinger_til_uddannelse_af_l_rere_og_p_dagoger.pdf","version":"Published V