{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Grabarczyk, Pawel","Freiesleben, Alma","Bastrup, Amanda","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382656"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computing educational programmes with more women are more about people amp less about things","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3502718.3524784","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382656","identifier":[{"id":"85134432652","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5cb7e261-83b0-439a-8362-c0841166e74e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E93C05C5C4D3B4FE9EBA47C02C2F1644"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3502718.3524784","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pawel","key":"grabarczykpau","last":"Grabarczyk","locid":"42147e05-f94c-471d-a889-c57a01e4bdd0","name":"Grabarczyk, Pawel","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-7474","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alma","key":"freieslebenpau","last":"Freiesleben","name":"Freiesleben, Alma","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Amanda","key":"bastruppau","last":"Bastrup","name":"Bastrup, Amanda","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781450392013"],"pages":"172-178","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ITiCSE 2022: Innovation and Technology in Computer Science Education (ITiCSE 2022)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134432652"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5cb7e261-83b0-439a-8362-c0841166e74e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computing Educational Programmes with more Women are more about People &amp; less about Things","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382656","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We present a long-term study of how university students experienced teaching/learning activities throughout the Covid-19 pandemic in Denmark1. We collected data through questionnaires from N=365 students enrolled in the “Intro- duction to Database Systems” course during four consecutive semesters (Spring 2020 to Fall 2021). The two years span the entire period of the pandemic’s interruption of normal on-site teaching, until restrictions were completely lifted in Denmark. The study investigates student preferences for online versus on- site teaching, and identifies the advantages of both, as well as changes in preferences throughout the pandemic. Quantitatively, the results demonstrate a preference for on-site over online teaching which was more pronounced for exercise classes than for lectures. Qualitatively, the study identifies several advantages of both online and on-site teaching; including a more engaging learning environment and better teacher-student interaction for on-site lectures, and flexibility and self-paced learning for online teaching. The primary changes identified were an increased sense of being able to focus online and a decrease in ease of asking questions online towards the later stages of the pandemic. Finally, we highlight the opportunity for universities to provide hybrid models of teaching, in order to care for diverse student preferences and needs.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jónsson, Björn Thór","Pischetola, Magda","Inie, Nanna","Daniels, Mats","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-430709"],"event":{"end":"2022-10-11","place":"Uppsala, se","start":"2022-10-08","title":"Frontiers in Education Conference 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Iceland","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Iceland","Uppsala University"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"student perspectives on on site versus online teaching throughout the covid 000000000019 pandemic","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/324956887/pandemic_pdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-430709","ids":["ku-3e610c3a-b6a4-4efe-a5be-4db9e2d18712"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CDC8301A8BB5EA064DC0633177DD51E9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/324956887/pandemic_pdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ccer.itu.dk/-/media/E166C300E514461E85C0EB6C89184197.ashx","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"is","key":"university of iceland","loc":["Iceland","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Iceland","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Björn Thór","key":"jónssonpau","last":"Jónsson","name":"Jónsson, Björn Thór","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Magda","key":"pischetolapau","last":"Pischetola","locid":"227e791f-6e3e-410c-afd5-0c6dcb56aab9","name":"Pischetola, Magda","orcid":"0000-0001-6697-2118","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","name":"Inie, Nanna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Mats","key":"danielspau","last":"Daniels","name":"Daniels, Mats","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","name":"Brabrand, Claus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3e610c3a-b6a4-4efe-a5be-4db9e2d18712"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Student Perspectives on On-site versus Online Teaching throughout the Covid-19 Pandemic","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-430709","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We present a long-term study of how university students experienced teaching/learning activities throughout the Covid-19 pandemic in Denmark 1 . We collected data through questionnaires from N=365 students enrolled in the \"Introduction to Database Systems\" course during four consecutive semesters (Spring 2020 to Fall 2021). The two years span the entire period of the pandemic’s interruption of normal on-site teaching, until restrictions were completely lifted in Denmark. The study investigates student preferences for online versus onsite teaching, and identifies the advantages of both, as well as changes in preferences throughout the pandemic. Quantitatively, the results demonstrate a preference for on-site over online teaching which was more pronounced for exercise classes than for lectures. Qualitatively, the study identifies several advantages of both online and on-site teaching; including a more engaging learning environment and better teacher-student interaction for on-site lectures, and flexibility and self-paced learning for online teaching. The primary changes identified were an increased sense of being able to focus online and a decrease in ease of asking questions online towards the later stages of the pandemic. Finally, we highlight the opportunity for universities to provide hybrid models of teaching, in order to care for diverse student preferences and needs.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jónsson, Björn Thór","Pischetola, Magda","Inie, Nanna","Daniels, Mats","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776383"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Hybrid teaching"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"student perspectives on on site versus online teaching throughout the covid 000000000019 pandemic","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106948081/Student_Perspectives_on_On_site_versus_O.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776383","identifier":[{"id":"85143784366","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2db9de83-cdb3-49bf-b3a8-f4468a1e1800"],"keyword":["Covid19 pandemic","hybrid teaching","online teaching and learning","student preferences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-960308C54A19D1837E9E82EBC88A6B29"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102946609/pandemic_pdf.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106948081/Student_Perspectives_on_On_site_versus_O.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://ccer.itu.dk/-/media/E166C300E514461E85C0EB6C89184197.ashx","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Björn Thór","key":"jónssonpau","last":"Jónsson","name":"Jónsson, Björn Thór","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Magda","key":"pischetolapau","last":"Pischetola","name":"Pischetola, Magda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mats","key":"danielspau","last":"Daniels","name":"Daniels, Mats","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/fie56618.2022.9962707","eisbn":["9781665462440"],"isbn":["9781665462457"],"pages":"1-9","place":"Uppsala, Sweden","series":"IEEE Frontiers in Education Conference","status":"p","title":"IEEE Frontiers in Education Conference (FIE 2022)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143784366"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2db9de83-cdb3-49bf-b3a8-f4468a1e1800"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Student Perspectives on On-site versus Online Teaching throughout the Covid-19 Pandemic","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776383","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: hospital admissions of residents from nursing homes often lead to delirium, infections, mortality and reduced functional capacity. We initiated a new service, 'emergency department-based acute care service', maintained by consultants from an emergency department (ED) moving emergency care from the hospitals into nursing homes. OBJECTIVE: this study explored healthcare professionals' experiences with this service. DESIGN: qualitative semi-structured focus group discussions. INTERVENTION/SETTING: the new service provides acute on-site evaluation and treatment to nursing home residents following calls to the emergency dispatch centre. METHODS: we conducted focus groups with general practitioners, prehospital personnel, municipal acute care nurses, ED staff and nursing home staff. The analysis was performed using the iterative and explorative approach, 'systematic text condensation'. RESULTS: the participants considered the service as a meaningful and appropriate alternative to hospital admission, as the treatment can be tailored to meet the residents' wishes and daily capabilities. This was experienced to promote dignity for the residents by reducing unnecessary transfers to the ED and the residents could remain in familiar surroundings with staff who knew their habitual behaviour and history. The nursing home staff contributed valuable information to the ED consultants' decision-making. The service made it possible to base the decision-making on complete patient pictures, as the ED consultants had the time to get to understand the residents. CONCLUSION: acute care at nursing homes provides an alternative to routine admissions to hospitals and enables healthcare professionals to provide more dignity in the care of nursing home residents.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Udesen, Stine Emilie Junker","Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","Andersen, Nina","Rasmussen, Claus-Henrik","Mikkelsen, Søren","Brabrand, Mikkel","Lassen, Annmarie Touborg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-600008"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Udesen, Stine Emilie Junker"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Odense Kommune"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"healthcare professionals experience with emergency department based acute care performed within nursing homes","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/219616921/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-600008","identifier":[{"id":"85136006599","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9385181","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35977148","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-5da7fd51-f6d3-4b1c-a253-67fa8d2bcfa7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-99DBEAA2B13D19698135AD213B185629"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/219616921/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://academic.oup.com/ageing/article/51/8/afac170/6670560","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9385181/pdf/afac170.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Emergency Medicine (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Odense Kommune"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Emilie Junker","key":"udesenpau","last":"Udesen","locid":"7552db96-a59d-4955-a83d-fde78472d168","name":"Udesen, Stine Emilie Junker","orcid":"0000-0002-5962-514X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe Susanne","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"52791e3c-f692-493c-9085-fd6de2c829ac","name":"Nielsen, Dorthe Susanne","orcid":"0000-0002-3954-7551","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Nina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus-Henrik","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3d4aa700-141d-4c3c-bfc5-d2d368cce808","name":"Rasmussen, Claus-Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"7df86a29-c6dc-4919-a9f9-6f5c23591e1d","name":"Mikkelsen, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-5187-7027","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"brabandpau","last":"Braband","locid":"96dae706-4310-46de-ac4f-447df19289f6","name":"Brabrand, Mikkel","name_org":"Braband, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0002-3340-8251","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annmarie","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"80e651b5-e70f-43e0-baf8-e88335ac10b8","name":"Lassen, Annmarie Touborg","name_org":"Lassen, Annmarie","orcid":"0000-0003-4942-6152","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35977148"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ageing/afac170","issn":["00020729","14682834"],"issn_org":["14682834"],"issue":"8","journal":"Age and Ageing","paperid":"afac170","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Age and Ageing","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136006599"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-5da7fd51-f6d3-4b1c-a253-67fa8d2bcfa7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Healthcare professionals' experience with emergency department-based acute care performed within nursing homes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-600008","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Dette dokument indeholder en række anbefalinger til indførsel af teknologiforståelse i uddannelse af lærere og andet pædagogisk personale i folkeskolen. Konkret drejer det sig om teknologiforståelse som selvstændigt fag og som element i de eksisterende fag matematik, billedkunst og håndværk og design. Anbefalingerne er udarbejdet af forskere og fageksperter fra universiteter og professionshøjskoler, der har deltaget i projekt ’Teknologiforståelse i uddannelse af lærere og andet pædagogisk personale’ under Børne- og Undervisningsministeriet. Projektet udgør 3. spor i ministeriets forsøgsprogram for teknologiforståelse i folkeskolens obligatoriske undervisning. Modsat forsøgsprojektets andre spor, der omhandler undervisning i folkeskolen, så omhandler spor 3 den faglighed, som lærere og lærerstuderende skal uddannes til på professionshøjskolerne for at kunne varetage undervisning i teknologiforståelse i skolens fag (hvad der kan betegnes som ’lærerfaglig teknologiforståelse’). Spor 3 berører således forholdet mellem skolefag og lærerfaglighed. Forskernes overordnede vurdering er, at forudsat opgaven med indførsel af teknologi forståelse i uddannelse af lærere og andet pædagogisk personale organiseres med hensyntagen til de afgivne anbefalinger, er der et betydeligt uddannelsesmæssigt potentiale i at indføre teknologiforståelse både som dyb selvstændig faglighed i eget fag og i flere variationer (teknologiforståelser) i fagene matematik, billedkunst og håndværk og design.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Andersen, Lars Bo","Brabrand, Claus","Buhl, Mie","Caprani, Ole","Georgsen, Marianne","Hachmann, Roland","Hjorth, Mikkel","Jørnø, Rasmus Leth","Køhrsen, Louis","Misfeldt, Morten","Nørgård, Rikke Toft","Nortvig, Anne-Mette","Rehder, Mads Middelboe"],"cuid":["S07-094.02-742101"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","corresponding_author":["Andersen, Lars Bo"],"ke